#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175684 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176037 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc2759a6-76b0-5410-b695-1e28b3168cb8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Marginal Distribution From a Joint Distribution: Non-Rectangular Domains"}] :question/id #uuid "b26c36dd-e371-5598-96a3-73fb1c147a7c" :question/math-academy-id "e-10048" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y) = 5y\\sqrt{x},  \\quad y^2 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\quad y\\geq 0.\n$$\n\nFind the expression for the marginal PDF $f_Y(y).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x, y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the region $D = \\{(x,y) \\::\\:   y^2 \\leq x \\leq1,\\, y\\geq 0 \\}.$\n\n![](images/4c/4c689a61af43d1d7aef57364a0d231256329305438e3fa046b048b7580fc13fe.png)\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $Y$ for $0 \\leq y \\leq 1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{1}5y\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5y{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{1}\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5y{[\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3/2}]}_{x={y}^{2}}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{10y}{3}{[{x}^{3/2}]}_{x={y}^{2}}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{10y}{3}[{1}^{3/2}-{({y}^{2})}^{3/2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{10y}{3}[1-{y}^{3}] \\\\  & =\\frac{10(y-{y}^{4})}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for $f_Y(y)$ is given by\n\n![](images/45/455169bc586c4c80c170a1ec5b8a831814f60e378ae56f471c0db75f439f6c36.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175852 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175999 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "62a2b5bc-ecf8-5e8e-bf4e-0cde666ec594" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Marginal Distribution From a Joint Distribution"}] :question/id #uuid "ed593b5a-be86-5f9a-b9a5-d82b07ed2cfd" :question/math-academy-id "e-9192" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n![](images/95/95ded6d2fba38750193e0b88b6c957dd841203590c6ce6ad493b19c31c76ac0b.svg)\nFind the expression for the marginal PDF $f_Y(y).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x, y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $Y$ for $0\\leq y \\leq1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{15}{7}{x}^{2}{y}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{7}{y}^{4}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{x=1}^{x=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{7}{y}^{4}[{x}^{3}]_{x=1}^{x=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{7}{y}^{4}({2}^{3}-{1}^{3}) \\\\  & =5{y}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for $f_Y(y)$ is given by\n\n![](images/14/140bdf82e603fcf61a0d217da56acd876bf97a88ef2f318e84a9477374ec3abe.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175853 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176000 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc918d1c-7446-59a5-ad73-f705f83ae49c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Marginal Probability From a Joint Distribution"}] :question/id #uuid "e0123816-b3f6-5fd4-a6ae-09c31bcce5cd" :question/math-academy-id "e-9193" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n![](images/a1/a1015cb8e8c7cd0bcee792c919b5f9c6f0e1ce180e971fcfeda8eecfc8238a47.svg)\nFind $P(-4 \\leq Y \\leq 4).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x, y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $Y$ for $y \\geq 0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-(4x+y/4)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{-(4x+y/4)}]}_{x=0}^{x=\\infty } \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}(0-{e}^{-(0+y/4)}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{-y/4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for $f_Y(y)$ is given by\n\n![](images/81/810669e70e34a95f937272d35174b4ccc72a5a3d6356a322893e516e7b6f4597.svg)\n\nTherefore, the required probability is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-4\\le Y\\le 4) & ={\\int }_{-4}^{4}{f}_{Y}(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{-y/4}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[-{e}^{-y/4}]}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =(-{e}^{-4/4}+{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{e}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175854 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176001 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ad789c4f-c4e1-5efc-8241-a55e4ac1dd07" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Marginal CDF"}] :question/id #uuid "acab7d19-e027-53cc-b491-58cbd73ee640" :question/math-academy-id "e-9195" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n![](images/38/38fbcd9603e79b21eb176e030a66ddf8d6a7e9e000c81b39987fa743380b92ea.svg)\n\nFind the marginal cumulative distribution function (CDF) $F_Y(y)$ of $Y.$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x, y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $Y$ for $-1 \\leq y \\leq 1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{3}{8}(x+y)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}{[\\frac{1}{3}(x+y)^{3}]}_{x=-1}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{[(x+y)^{3}]}_{x=-1}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}[(1+y)^{3}-(-1+y)^{3}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}[(y+1)^{3}-(y-1)^{3}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}[({y}^{3}+3{y}^{2}+3y+1)-({y}^{3}-3{y}^{2}+3y-1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}[(\\cancel{{y}^{3}}+3{y}^{2}+\\cancel{3y}+1)-(\\cancel{{y}^{3}}-3{y}^{2}+\\cancel{3y}-1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}[2(3{y}^{2}+1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(3{y}^{2}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the marginal CDF of $Y$ for $-1 \\leq y \\leq 1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{y}{f}_{Y}(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{y}\\frac{1}{4}(3{u}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{-1}^{y}(3{u}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{[{u}^{3}+u]}_{-1}^{y} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[{y}^{3}+y-(-1)^{3}-(-1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[{y}^{3}+y+2] \\\\  & =\\frac{{y}^{3}+y+2}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for the marginal CDF of $Y$ is\n\n![](images/0a/0a44179f2169e2c2660c6bb6e5bb23d5298786ee5d3f0fb181c3b71bf61ca0fe.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176258 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175999 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "62a2b5bc-ecf8-5e8e-bf4e-0cde666ec594" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Marginal Distribution From a Joint Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0df9164a-2aee-5ef0-b081-85127f1a8451" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{7}{y}^{2}, & 1\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476226} {:answer/id #uuid "1c514f66-29f0-5f0b-bfe0-72c4620d0193" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{3}y, & 1\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476264} {:answer/id #uuid "6d3e17cd-c3c8-537b-b290-5a1e7b10eed5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}y, & 1\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476446} {:answer/id #uuid "920faada-7711-5c7e-870a-65e8a1d7f033" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}y, & 1\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476516} {:answer/id #uuid "b2852486-2a3e-5a1c-8255-69aa2ae0c1fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1, & 1\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476604}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d3e17cd-c3c8-537b-b290-5a1e7b10eed5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}y, & 1\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476446} :answer-field/id #uuid "94e671b2-3bc6-5214-829c-28d39395095c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186173806}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "299fe748-fc78-5066-b383-fe1227671e5c" :question/math-academy-id "q-110409" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8}{3}{x}^{3}y, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,1\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the expression for the marginal PDF ${f}_{Y}(y).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $Y$ for $1\\le y\\le 2$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{8}{3}{x}^{3}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}y{[\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}y[{x}^{4}]_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}y({1}^{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}y, & 1\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176261 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176000 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc918d1c-7446-59a5-ad73-f705f83ae49c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Marginal Probability From a Joint Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "855080ee-7d77-5608-a727-98aeca63c799" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.896" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186173825} {:answer/id #uuid "d5c74169-51d2-5344-a44b-da35014e75ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.104" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186173826} {:answer/id #uuid "e9b25d28-14c6-5d5a-b7ed-d5edc59b963e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.658" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186173827} {:answer/id #uuid "515d0182-6f19-53ef-9998-81b80b6bb6e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.205" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186173828} {:answer/id #uuid "7f7cb9cc-8702-5b2b-b64d-27610d91deb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.342" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186173829}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "855080ee-7d77-5608-a727-98aeca63c799" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.896" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186173825} :answer-field/id #uuid "8dd4eda8-fb5d-5a1b-b8c6-e12059aeaa19" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186173824}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5dd8d5b2-3566-50a9-8091-3b7c245239df" :question/math-academy-id "q-110417" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}), & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(0.2<X<1).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $X$ for $0\\le x\\le 1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x) & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3}{2}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}y+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =[\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}]-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for ${f}_{X}(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}, & 0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the required probability is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0.2<X<1) & ={\\int }_{0.2}^{1}{f}_{X}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0.2}^{1}(\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}x]}_{0.2}^{1} \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{2}(1)^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}(1)]-[\\frac{1}{2}(0.2)^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}(0.2)] \\\\  & =1-0.104 \\\\  & =0.896.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476947 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176037 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc2759a6-76b0-5410-b695-1e28b3168cb8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Marginal Distribution From a Joint Distribution: Non-Rectangular Domains"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fd49525-ce7b-5de7-bb4b-853ca8c7b51d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}6{y}^{2}-3{y}^{3}, & 0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476308} {:answer/id #uuid "5f91b3ea-874f-54c6-9b5a-27d6749d139c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}^{3}, & 0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476417} {:answer/id #uuid "8b2b6b61-00a6-5cd5-b748-9e114f816504" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1+{y}^{2}+{y}^{3}, & 0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476504} {:answer/id #uuid "9fd12cd1-d9b6-5434-b061-5a342e650a92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1+3{y}^{2}-4{y}^{3}, & 0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476548} {:answer/id #uuid "d5462deb-905b-5315-b5e7-9ee7d87bb3b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3+{y}^{2}-4{y}^{3}, & 0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476680}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d5462deb-905b-5315-b5e7-9ee7d87bb3b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3+{y}^{2}-4{y}^{3}, & 0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476680} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f4e6988-a890-5061-983b-4ccf67591ee4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476817}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b503f4b2-2e6a-599e-9f9e-bfcbf92fe455" :question/math-academy-id "q-142710" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with a joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{3},\\,0\\le 3y\\le x\\le 3.\n$$\n\nFind the expression for the marginal PDF ${f}_{Y}(y).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the region $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le 3y\\le x\\le 3\\}.$\n\n![](images/54/54c803be9ecc7873f2624fc9d083997039cb651c11cc38eff6fa561ec064b7a5.png)\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $Y$ for $0\\le y\\le 1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{3y}^{3}\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{3y}^{3}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+x{y}^{2}]}_{x=3y}^{x=3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {3}^{3}+3\\cdot {y}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}(3y)^{3}-3y\\cdot {y}^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[9+3{y}^{2}-12{y}^{3}] \\\\  & =3+{y}^{2}-4{y}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3+{y}^{2}-4{y}^{3}, & 0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476940 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175999 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "62a2b5bc-ecf8-5e8e-bf4e-0cde666ec594" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Marginal Distribution From a Joint Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17aadaf2-4ba7-5796-a001-c0bbe9dcac22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+\\frac{2}{3}, & 0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476242} {:answer/id #uuid "3d8a0898-7457-5d87-af4d-85f0fb6d7665" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4x+1}{3}, & 0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476338} {:answer/id #uuid "9f32af68-e5ee-55a4-9cfe-8d1f23989236" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+x, & 0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476546} {:answer/id #uuid "bea7ae9e-7458-5741-9279-66e4924e7c75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8}{9}, & 0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476638} {:answer/id #uuid "c6feae73-dcc8-57f0-b4da-622fffd1cf65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+\\frac{4}{3}x, & 0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476651}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6feae73-dcc8-57f0-b4da-622fffd1cf65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+\\frac{4}{3}x, & 0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476651} :answer-field/id #uuid "b821f73d-7070-57a0-ab5a-2ac12f5bc93f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476837}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "acc3ecee-2ca3-52a4-a564-fe35d9f4b095" :question/math-academy-id "q-142754" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+\\frac{8}{9}xy, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,1\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the expression for the marginal PDF ${f}_{X}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $X$ for $0\\le x\\le 1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x) & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}({x}^{2}+\\frac{8}{9}xy)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[{x}^{2}y+\\frac{4}{9}x{y}^{2}]}_{y=1}^{y=2} \\\\  & =({x}^{2}(2)+\\frac{4}{9}x\\cdot {2}^{2})-({x}^{2}(1)+\\frac{4}{9}x\\cdot {1}^{2}) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+\\frac{4}{3}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for ${f}_{X}(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+\\frac{4}{3}x, & 0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176364 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176037 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc2759a6-76b0-5410-b695-1e28b3168cb8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Marginal Distribution From a Joint Distribution: Non-Rectangular Domains"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e1c2488-6f19-5f75-8228-75b61035e030" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\frac{1}{\\pi ({y}^{2}+1)}\\,,\\,-\\infty <y<\\infty \\,." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476227} {:answer/id #uuid "1961d4db-fe56-563a-9283-1c81c4dc846c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,,\\,-\\infty <y<\\infty \\,." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476247} {:answer/id #uuid "82eb8742-36e7-5ffd-a6f6-69aaa4ab4057" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\pi }}\\,{e}^{-{y}^{2}}\\,,\\,-\\infty <y<\\infty \\,." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476492} {:answer/id #uuid "9558bd26-9177-5a95-ae61-67abc43f1a3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)={e}^{-{y}^{2}}\\,,\\,-\\infty <y<\\infty \\,." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476522} {:answer/id #uuid "95a54a82-53ef-52bd-a12a-f81380aaff75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\frac{2}{\\pi (4{y}^{4}+1)}\\,,\\,-\\infty <y<\\infty \\,." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476524}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e1c2488-6f19-5f75-8228-75b61035e030" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\frac{1}{\\pi ({y}^{2}+1)}\\,,\\,-\\infty <y<\\infty \\,." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476227} :answer-field/id #uuid "a96ed7e6-c50b-50a2-b3e6-536e5dec7124" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174442}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "19e2e9e5-da57-56e4-b48b-5d2aa326a248" :question/math-academy-id "q-142856" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with a joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\frac{1}{\\pi {x}^{2}},\\,{y}^{2}+1\\le x.\n$$\n\nFind the expression for the marginal PDF ${f}_{Y}(y).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the region $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,{y}^{2}+1\\le x\\}.$\n\n![](images/0a/0a75ec87c30ea5708201cb76816ea3a806648cec197195994cafbe9d9cf588d1.png)\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $Y$ for $-\\infty <y<\\infty $ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{{y}^{2}+1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{\\pi {x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{{y}^{2}+1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{lim}_{b\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{{y}^{2}+1}^{b}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{lim}_{b\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{1}{x}]}_{x={y}^{2}+1}^{x=b} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\pi }{lim}_{b\\to \\infty }[\\frac{1}{b}-\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}+1}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\pi }[0-\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}+1}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi ({y}^{2}+1)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\frac{1}{\\pi ({y}^{2}+1)}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476875 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176001 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ad789c4f-c4e1-5efc-8241-a55e4ac1dd07" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Marginal CDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "141b8f61-deff-5934-b9c3-910770639c5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476235} {:answer/id #uuid "35b1ba0b-b624-5ab8-b04e-b638b43bbe11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476322} {:answer/id #uuid "471383ca-dfca-562f-871b-65f52c3bf25c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476354} {:answer/id #uuid "f1599fb6-22fd-570f-a8e0-dcdc16c9cddc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476739} {:answer/id #uuid "f61eda3e-11f8-5e7b-9353-d73bdfe137ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476745}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "471383ca-dfca-562f-871b-65f52c3bf25c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476354} :answer-field/id #uuid "efcde246-3b99-5c3b-9257-5e8e1919f2e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476862}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "076df80a-4584-5238-8a7e-ff37062cbf3b" :question/math-academy-id "q-142857" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2y, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe marginal CDF ${F}_{X}(x)$ of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n{F}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ g(x), & 0\\le x\\le 1 \\\\ 1 & x>1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhat is the function $g(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $X$ for $0\\le x\\le 1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x) & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2{[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =[{y}^{2}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =({1}^{2}-0) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the marginal CDF of $X$ for $0\\le x\\le 1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}_{X}(x) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}{f}_{X}(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{x}1\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =[u]_{0}^{x} \\\\  & =x-0 \\\\  & =x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the full expression for ${F}_{X}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{F}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ x, & 0\\le x\\le 1 \\\\ 1 & x>1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $g(x)=x.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476889 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176001 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ad789c4f-c4e1-5efc-8241-a55e4ac1dd07" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Marginal CDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "080ba9b9-8963-507d-b891-91fccbf687c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-{e}^{-y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476216} {:answer/id #uuid "28302a4c-381c-5184-8bf7-1a2de35cc31a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{{y}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476294} {:answer/id #uuid "3720d3c5-7d4d-5275-98de-8c62924defdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476325} {:answer/id #uuid "6d1d0f0d-8129-5494-8892-c2b298041668" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476445} {:answer/id #uuid "e9e9020e-860d-5a4e-a5c5-8098b6ef2473" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-{e}^{-{y}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476725}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3720d3c5-7d4d-5275-98de-8c62924defdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476325} :answer-field/id #uuid "057d939c-b8eb-5a5d-bd62-0bb22aaeb85f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476762}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4107781e-c996-571c-b9f1-cc16eec90a01" :question/math-academy-id "q-142861" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x+y}, & x\\le 0,\\,y\\le 0, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe marginal CDF ${F}_{Y}(y)$ of $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\n{F}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}g(y), & y\\le 0 \\\\ 1 & y>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhat is the function $g(y)?$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $Y$ for $y\\le 0$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{y}{lim}_{b\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{b}^{0}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{y}{lim}_{b\\to -\\infty }{[{e}^{x}]}_{b}^{0} \\\\  & ={e}^{y}{lim}_{b\\to -\\infty }(1-{e}^{b}) \\\\  & ={e}^{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the marginal CDF of $Y$ for $y\\le 0$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{y}{f}_{Y}(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{y}{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={lim}_{b\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{b}^{y}{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={lim}_{b\\to -\\infty }{[{e}^{u}]}_{b}^{y} \\\\  & ={lim}_{b\\to -\\infty }({e}^{y}-{e}^{b}) \\\\  & ={e}^{y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the full expression for ${F}_{Y}(y)$ is\n\n$$\n{F}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{y}, & y\\le 0 \\\\ 1 & y>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $g(y)={e}^{y}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476913 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175999 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "62a2b5bc-ecf8-5e8e-bf4e-0cde666ec594" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Marginal Distribution From a Joint Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e97b129-580d-59cf-b93d-a5f15b4a69f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{1-\\sqrt{2}}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y), & 0\\le y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476450} {:answer/id #uuid "96202c10-895a-5653-9141-10869b52646e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{1-\\sqrt{2}}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}+y)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y), & 0\\le y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476528} {:answer/id #uuid "a0ede3e4-6cd5-51ec-a66b-65ac756d3972" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}-1}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}+y)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y), & 0\\le y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476555} {:answer/id #uuid "cb40a145-d832-5c0d-b590-7a7995459d68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{1-\\sqrt{2}}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y), & 0\\le y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476661} {:answer/id #uuid "eabdea2d-66a4-530f-bf9f-3cb5839040be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}-1}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}+y)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y), & 0\\le y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476727}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eabdea2d-66a4-530f-bf9f-3cb5839040be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}-1}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}+y)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y), & 0\\le y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476727} :answer-field/id #uuid "7fc4e10a-30c9-5bff-b8a6-df1e61c3c7b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476813}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7462dbdf-074b-5e9c-88bb-4a4709315e55" :question/math-academy-id "q-142872" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}-1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y), & 0\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4},\\,0\\le y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the expression for the marginal PDF ${f}_{Y}(y).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $Y$ for $0\\le y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}-1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}-1}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)]_{x=0}^{x=\\pi /4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}-1}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}+y)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0+y)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}-1}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}+y)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}-1}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}+y)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y), & 0\\le y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476931 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175999 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "62a2b5bc-ecf8-5e8e-bf4e-0cde666ec594" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Marginal Distribution From a Joint Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5351eae7-dc6c-5a57-81bb-251115e032a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}y+\\frac{1}{2}, & 0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476378} {:answer/id #uuid "63acac21-1914-55df-8f46-e1df0c572d17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}y+2, & 0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476429} {:answer/id #uuid "6b5cfbf8-b34e-5c08-942c-fd1b4c89d51b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1, & 0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476443} {:answer/id #uuid "ae7225b6-8f8a-507a-869b-7e8fc526e349" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}y, & 0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476590} {:answer/id #uuid "fbad6de2-e944-5d9d-8691-ad17c4fe0fbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2y, & 0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476753}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5351eae7-dc6c-5a57-81bb-251115e032a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}y+\\frac{1}{2}, & 0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476378} :answer-field/id #uuid "edc25465-db53-5da9-ab78-ec9a5725f2c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476858}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a1209ac5-9324-5c4f-8a14-c5d815ce9e79" :question/math-academy-id "q-142888" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the expression for the marginal PDF ${f}_{Y}(y).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $Y$ for $0\\le y\\le 1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(x+y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+xy]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =[(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {1}^{2}+1\\cdot y)-(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {0}^{2}+0\\cdot y)] \\\\  & =y+\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}y+\\frac{1}{2}, & 0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476942 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176000 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc918d1c-7446-59a5-ad73-f705f83ae49c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Marginal Probability From a Joint Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72270fd2-6992-5f31-97a2-2ca4ee17ded5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{1}{{e}^{25}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476461} {:answer/id #uuid "7ced4ceb-454c-52c6-af4d-6e2ad83dfe18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{25}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476480} {:answer/id #uuid "968b508d-00d7-5293-968a-76a5988b5ac5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{1}{{e}^{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476531} {:answer/id #uuid "a976e357-0ba9-5d47-9790-62cdf8d6dbdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{5}}-\\frac{1}{{e}^{25}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476576} {:answer/id #uuid "b606dc72-4cfc-5e8f-9fe7-991ba2e0b461" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476616}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72270fd2-6992-5f31-97a2-2ca4ee17ded5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{1}{{e}^{25}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476461} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b857419-f18b-50b2-bb98-09131889cb3e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476802}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "aecec449-e3ae-5803-8a70-f99f6be91bad" :question/math-academy-id "q-142911" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-(5x+\\frac{y}{5})}, & x\\ge 0,\\,y\\ge 0, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(X\\le 5).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $X$ for $x\\ge 0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-(5x+\\frac{y}{5})}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[-5{e}^{-(5x+\\frac{y}{5})}]}_{y=0}^{y=\\infty } \\\\  & =-5(0-{e}^{-(5x+0)}) \\\\  & =5{e}^{-5x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for ${f}_{X}(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}5{e}^{-5x}, & x\\ge 0, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the required probability is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 5) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{5}{f}_{X}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{5}5{e}^{-5x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-{e}^{-5x}]}_{0}^{5} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-25}+{e}^{0} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{{e}^{25}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476914 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176001 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ad789c4f-c4e1-5efc-8241-a55e4ac1dd07" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Marginal CDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a53314f-f55e-5de3-9361-255122ecd28d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476251} {:answer/id #uuid "1f7ed870-0b8d-550d-abc6-3a5002277034" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{y}^{3/2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476272} {:answer/id #uuid "20349e86-f87d-5afc-84ce-b2382a2a6350" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476276} {:answer/id #uuid "59076299-fa05-510b-bc19-29ea93c3586f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476392} {:answer/id #uuid "9c74adee-37f0-5906-921a-264e40407fe1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476542}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c74adee-37f0-5906-921a-264e40407fe1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476542} :answer-field/id #uuid "9146ede4-3856-5d3a-8193-cdcf33cf5f1c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476819}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "74d58075-0369-56a0-b633-ba74268879be" :question/math-academy-id "q-142916" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y\\sqrt{x}}{9}, & 0\\le x\\le 9,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe marginal CDF ${F}_{Y}(y)$ of $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\n{F}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & y<0 \\\\ g(y), & 0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 1 & y>1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhat is the function $g(y)?$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $Y$ for $0\\le y\\le 1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{0}^{9}\\frac{y\\sqrt{x}}{9}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{9}\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{9}{[\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3/2}]}_{x=0}^{x=9} \\\\  & =\\frac{2y}{27}{[{x}^{3/2}]}_{x=0}^{x=9} \\\\  & =\\frac{2y}{27}({9}^{3/2}-{0}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2y}{27}(27-0) \\\\  & =2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the marginal CDF of $Y$ for $0\\le y\\le 1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{y}{f}_{Y}(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{y}2u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={[{u}^{2}]}_{0}^{y} \\\\  & ={y}^{2}-0 \\\\  & ={y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the full expression for ${F}_{Y}(y)$ is\n\n$$\n{F}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & y<0 \\\\ {y}^{2}, & 0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 1 & y>1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $g(y)={y}^{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476884 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176001 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ad789c4f-c4e1-5efc-8241-a55e4ac1dd07" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Marginal CDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "657be62f-e6cf-5e98-b0fe-061ed0c317ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476432} {:answer/id #uuid "7e8bf4a0-5dfd-5230-8dc4-539d957d5aa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x-1}{x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476482} {:answer/id #uuid "91cec410-3544-5b99-84ab-6aa46c4443e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476515} {:answer/id #uuid "b4e7a5c1-ac85-558b-941d-74d5104f775a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{(x+1)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476614} {:answer/id #uuid "dcf8e657-8c89-50bd-98b0-b327d64295c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x-1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476701}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e8bf4a0-5dfd-5230-8dc4-539d957d5aa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x-1}{x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476482} :answer-field/id #uuid "7592e58e-c6d2-57f8-87f1-5cf59d6709fe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476809}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "31433c7d-56df-5a56-80c3-21c7e39be82f" :question/math-academy-id "q-142923" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{(x+y)^{3}}, & x\\ge 1,\\,y\\ge 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe marginal CDF ${F}_{X}(x)$ of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n{F}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\\\ g(x), & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhat is the function $g(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $X$ for $x\\ge 1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x) & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{4}{(x+y)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={lim}_{b\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{b}\\frac{4}{(x+y)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =4{lim}_{b\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{b}(x+y)^{-3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =4{lim}_{b\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{1}{2}(x+y)^{-2}]}_{y=1}^{y=b} \\\\  & =-2{lim}_{b\\to \\infty }{[\\frac{1}{(x+y)^{2}}]}_{y=1}^{y=b} \\\\  & =-2{lim}_{b\\to \\infty }[\\frac{1}{(x+b)^{2}}-\\frac{1}{(x+1)^{2}}] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{(x+1)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the marginal CDF of $X$ for $x\\ge 1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}_{X}(x) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}{f}_{X}(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{x}\\frac{2}{(u+1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{1}^{x}\\frac{1}{(u+1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2{[-\\frac{1}{u+1}]}_{1}^{x} \\\\  & =2[\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{x+1}] \\\\  & =1-\\frac{2}{x+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{x-1}{x+1},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the full expression for ${F}_{X}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{F}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\\\ \\frac{x-1}{x+1}, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $g(x)=\\frac{x-1}{x+1}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476948 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176001 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ad789c4f-c4e1-5efc-8241-a55e4ac1dd07" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Marginal CDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19e05135-dc72-54d1-a265-7303f0c55750" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476249} {:answer/id #uuid "2a48b4c7-e269-5b07-a4ea-37ff96fee042" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476299} {:answer/id #uuid "772175ea-626c-579e-9d22-f7b5ba8cba19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476471} {:answer/id #uuid "b8329249-ead1-5e17-95ed-e5b59ee76c7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}-1}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476620} {:answer/id #uuid "c9e5ae14-8d9d-5fd7-be35-533fed06278b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x-1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476656}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c9e5ae14-8d9d-5fd7-be35-533fed06278b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x-1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476656} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b5eb91d-c108-5a2b-99e3-c07f16397e3a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476823}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b66f8317-7401-5c42-a057-174f43015e08" :question/math-academy-id "q-142924" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}, & x\\ge 1,\\,y\\ge 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe marginal CDF ${F}_{X}(x)$ of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n{F}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\\\ g(x), & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhat is the function $g(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $X$ for $x\\ge 1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x) & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}{lim}_{b\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{b}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}{lim}_{b\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{1}{y}]}_{y=1}^{y=b} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}{lim}_{b\\to \\infty }[1-\\frac{1}{b}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the marginal CDF of $X$ for $x\\ge 1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}_{X}(x) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}{f}_{X}(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{x}\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{u}]}_{1}^{x} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{x-1}{x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the full expression for ${F}_{X}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{F}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\\\ \\frac{x-1}{x}, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $g(x)=\\frac{x-1}{x}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476954 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176000 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc918d1c-7446-59a5-ad73-f705f83ae49c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Marginal Probability From a Joint Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "320d3cb5-bef1-53b0-95c4-cff9ede43030" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{27}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476314} {:answer/id #uuid "4af6259e-a55c-5863-973f-a60c2eba3557" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{26}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476358} {:answer/id #uuid "95ffaac9-33b1-5d66-82ac-051de97f1e95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{20}{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476527} {:answer/id #uuid "bd15e8ea-65f0-52e8-8cf8-066dd559eb76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476633} {:answer/id #uuid "f5587a79-ea8a-50f2-8937-9dd583bde64d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{26}{27}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476743}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f5587a79-ea8a-50f2-8937-9dd583bde64d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{26}{27}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476743} :answer-field/id #uuid "341d4747-e282-5d0e-9b1a-d8cec6a359cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476781}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bdb3668b-11de-51d3-b228-d2e5f99dedeb" :question/math-academy-id "q-142951" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{21}(xy)^{2}, & 0\\le x\\le 3,\\,1\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(X>1).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $X$ for $0\\le x\\le 3$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x) & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{21}(xy)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{21}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{21}{[\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{y=1}^{y=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{63}({2}^{3}-{1}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for ${f}_{X}(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{9}{x}^{2}, & 0\\le x\\le 3, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the required probability is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>1) & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{f}_{X}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{1}{9}{x}^{2}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{27}[{3}^{3}-{1}^{3}] \\\\  & =\\frac{26}{27}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476885 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176000 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc918d1c-7446-59a5-ad73-f705f83ae49c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Marginal Probability From a Joint Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "227e60f3-8280-5cbf-8272-817ecc9418b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476281} {:answer/id #uuid "319584c3-1568-5dd4-b6cb-a605a46cc20e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476313} {:answer/id #uuid "87cba462-a4d6-545c-b338-05c85b3893b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476500} {:answer/id #uuid "a7c99b52-b19c-5699-807a-a3d706a7ca87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476572} {:answer/id #uuid "abe55a60-f081-501a-9966-badc5cf81888" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476585}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "319584c3-1568-5dd4-b6cb-a605a46cc20e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476313} :answer-field/id #uuid "e40af03a-e8f7-59d9-84b2-010d7a830506" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476856}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "335726b7-e5f3-5cb6-916f-382cd146373a" :question/math-academy-id "q-142965" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-(\\frac{x}{2}+2y)}, & x\\ge 0,\\,y\\ge 0, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(Y>2).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $Y$ for $y\\ge 0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-(\\frac{x}{2}+2y)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-2{e}^{-(\\frac{x}{2}+2y)}]}_{x=0}^{x=\\infty } \\\\  & =-2(0-{e}^{-(0+2y)}) \\\\  & =2{e}^{-2y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{-2y}, & y\\ge 0, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required probability is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y>2) & ={\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }{f}_{Y}(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }2{e}^{-2y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[-{e}^{-2y}]}_{2}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =(0+{e}^{-4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476909 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176000 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc918d1c-7446-59a5-ad73-f705f83ae49c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Marginal Probability From a Joint Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11448eff-f99f-5d32-8404-040f21de29d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4142" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476230} {:answer/id #uuid "39635364-1829-582d-9bac-a7ed3b6b80b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476333} {:answer/id #uuid "a52fb077-31e9-5727-8a98-141723176b5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7071" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476565} {:answer/id #uuid "b0bf5ad0-1aef-5e73-ad2f-7de86ffb5a37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4177" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476598} {:answer/id #uuid "fde49b78-51ae-5a61-b50d-18027829e3e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476757}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0bf5ad0-1aef-5e73-ad2f-7de86ffb5a37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4177" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476598} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c6cde9b-2e7a-54f6-a96c-10b188d72d9e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476826}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6d033f40-c93e-54e7-8136-01042b0b61b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-142967" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}-1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y), & 0\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4},\\,0\\le y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(-\\frac{\\pi }{6}<Y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{12}).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $Y$ for $0\\le y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}-1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}-1}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)]_{x=0}^{x=\\pi /4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}-1}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}+y)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0+y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}-1}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}+y)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}-1}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}+y)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y), & 0\\le y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required probability is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-\\frac{\\pi }{6}<Y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{12}) & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /6}^{\\pi /12}{f}_{Y}(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /12}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}-1}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}+y)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}-1}{[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}+y)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡y]}_{0}^{\\pi /12} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}-1}[(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{\\pi }{12})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{12})-(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}+0)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡0)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}-1}(-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1+\\sqrt{3}}{2\\sqrt{2}}+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-1) \\\\  & ≈0.4177.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476911 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175999 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "62a2b5bc-ecf8-5e8e-bf4e-0cde666ec594" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Marginal Distribution From a Joint Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16434b6b-ea07-586f-9f24-fb4740ac451b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2y}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476240} {:answer/id #uuid "8802a72a-be9c-51d8-a106-ffd3f5b13ac0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476502} {:answer/id #uuid "99847d23-9b4c-53fc-a600-f122a9064fb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476538} {:answer/id #uuid "c422b694-0161-5bfa-8a84-689ca1acfe8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476645} {:answer/id #uuid "fbb479f7-47d7-58d7-9bbf-b210d2c38e12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{y}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476754}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99847d23-9b4c-53fc-a600-f122a9064fb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476538} :answer-field/id #uuid "fcdfbcb7-b6c6-5e73-9143-d0c9ce607525" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476868}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7040e2bd-4a32-5fec-9df4-e31bdd95ffae" :question/math-academy-id "q-145015" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x{y}^{2}}{4}, & \\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 2 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the expression for the marginal PDF ${f}_{Y}(y).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $Y$ for $0\\le y\\le 2$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{x{y}^{2}}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}{\\int }_{1}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{x=1}^{x=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}[2-\\frac{1}{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{8}, & \\,0\\le y\\le 2 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
